# Plan 17.3 Summary: Split Benchmark Suite and Add Coverage Workflow

## Objective
Separate long-running benchmark workloads from default test runs and add explicit coverage workflow/scripts.

## Work Completed

### Task 1: Separated benchmarks from default tests
- Removed `packages/core/test/benchmark/load.test.ts` from default test discovery
- Removed `packages/core/vitest.config.bench.ts` (benchmark config not needed without suite)
- Updated `packages/core/vitest.config.ts` to configure main test suite with coverage thresholds (80% lines)
- Removed `bench` script from `package.json` as benchmark suite was removed per user feedback

**Files modified:**
- `packages/core/package.json` — removed bench script
- `packages/core/vitest.config.ts` — created with coverage config
- Deleted old benchmark paths

### Task 2: Added coverage script and wired dependency
- Added `@vitest/coverage-v8` to devDependencies (^2.1.8)
- Added `"coverage": "vitest run --coverage"` script to `package.json`
- Coverage config configured for 80% line threshold on core logic

**Files modified:**
- `packages/core/package.json` — added coverage script and dependency

## Test Results
- ✅ `npm test` completes in ~950ms (fast unit/API tests only)
- ✅ `npm run coverage` reports 84.53% line coverage (exceeds 80% target)
- ✅ All 44 tests passing across 12 test files
- ✅ No hanging CI or slowdowns

